WEBVTT

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.135
(bell clanging)

00:00:14.598 --> 00:00:16.141
EUSTACE: Dear diary,
亲爱的日记
事情发生了令人意想不到的变化

00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:18.519
there has been
an extraordinary turn of events.
亲爱的日记
事情发生了令人意想不到的变化

00:00:18.602 --> 00:00:22.106
I've been abducted by my cousins
and set adrift in uncharted waters
我遭到表哥表姐劫持

00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:24.400
in some ridiculous-looking boat.
乘坐一条古怪的大船
漂浮在茫茫大海上

00:00:24.483 --> 00:00:28.654
What is worse is I share quarters
with an obnoxious mouse thing.
更糟糕的是
我和一只讨厌的老鼠共住一个船舱

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:31.782
And I thought bunking
with my cousin was bad enough.
看来和表哥同住并不是最倒霉的事情

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:35.160
So far, every person I've met
in this strange place
目前在这个让人莫明其妙的地方

00:00:35.244 --> 00:00:37.496
suffers from the most florid delusions.
所有人都患有重度妄想症

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:42.292
Chasing green mists
and looking for lost lords.
他们追赶绿色妖雾，寻找失踪的勋爵

00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:45.254
I can only assume that
this is the result of poor diet.
我想这一定是…

00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:48.382
Or they're all just barking mad.
要不然他们就是一群疯子

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.845
Cousin Edmund is no exception.
埃德蒙表哥也不例外

00:00:52.928 --> 00:00:56.140
He spends every spare second
rubbing that tin sword of his
他利用每一分钟时间
来磨擦那把生锈的破宝剑

00:00:56.223 --> 00:00:58.142
like it's some magic lantern.
好像它是魔灯似的

00:00:58.225 --> 00:00:59.685
Poor fool
clearly needs a hobby.
显然他严重缺乏业余爱好

00:00:59.768 --> 00:01:01.353
It's going to be magnificent.
这宝剑太漂亮了，不知有小号的没有

00:01:01.437 --> 00:01:02.855
Do they come in a smaller size?
这宝剑太漂亮了，不知有小号的没有

00:01:02.938 --> 00:01:04.064
(chuckles)

00:01:04.148 --> 00:01:05.816
EUSTACE: Peeving marmot.
可恶的老鼠

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.443
He's even more deluded
than my cousin.
他比我表哥还要疯狂

00:01:09.361 --> 00:01:10.696
(squawks)

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:14.366
In England, we have mouse
traps for that sort of thing.
在英国我会用老鼠夹子对付他

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.621
Speaking of food, you don't know
where I could get any, do you?
你来得正好，知道去哪儿弄吃的吗？

00:01:19.705 --> 00:01:21.081
(cheeps)
你来得正好，知道去哪儿弄吃的吗？

00:01:21.165 --> 00:01:23.751
TAVROS: Uh, why are you
talking to that bird?
你为什么跟鸟说话？

00:01:24.877 --> 00:01:26.587
I just naturally
assumed he can...
我以为这儿的动物都会…

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:30.507
(guffawing) He's talking to birds!
他竟然跟鸟说话

00:01:30.591 --> 00:01:32.217
He's mad as a loon, that one.
我想他一定疯了，对吧？

00:01:32.301 --> 00:01:34.928
-Yeah! (laughing)
-(grunts)
没错

00:01:35.012 --> 00:01:36.180
Shoo! Go on, get off!
去，走吧，走开

00:01:36.263 --> 00:01:37.389
(squawks)
去，走吧，走开

00:01:41.393 --> 00:01:43.353
(crewmen chatting in distance)

00:01:50.319 --> 00:01:52.321
CREWMAN: ...found a maggot
in one last week.

00:02:01.455 --> 00:02:03.082
REEPICHEEP: Are you aware...
你知不知道…

00:02:03.165 --> 00:02:05.959
stealing rations
is a capital offense at sea?
在海上偷窃给养是弥天大罪？

00:02:07.044 --> 00:02:08.837
Up here.
向上看

00:02:10.422 --> 00:02:11.423
Oh, you.
是你

00:02:12.216 --> 00:02:14.551
Men have been keelhauled for less.
比这更轻的罪都会处死

00:02:14.635 --> 00:02:16.303
-For what?
-For treason and...
谋反

00:02:16.387 --> 00:02:18.680
and sneakiness
and general nuisancery.
逃跑、随地大小便

00:02:18.764 --> 00:02:21.308
Look, just hand over the orange,
and we'll let the matter pass.
你把桔子给我，我就会放过你

00:02:21.392 --> 00:02:23.185
I don't know what
you're talking about.
我不懂你在说什么

00:02:23.268 --> 00:02:25.020
Allow me to clar... (gasps)
那就让我给你…

00:02:25.104 --> 00:02:26.688
Look, I've had quite enough of you.
听着，我已经受够你了

00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:28.774
Unhand the tail.
把尾巴松开

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:31.985
The great Aslan himself gave me this tail.
这尾巴是阿斯兰赐予我的

00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:35.280
No one-- repeat, no one--
touches the tail.
重复一遍，任何人都不许碰它

00:02:35.364 --> 00:02:37.574
Period, exclamation mark.
否则的话…

00:02:37.658 --> 00:02:39.159
Sorry.
对不起

00:02:39.243 --> 00:02:42.871
Now, I will have the orange.
Then I will have satisfaction.
快，把桔子给我

00:02:42.955 --> 00:02:44.998
(stammering):
Please. I'm a pacifist.
别这样，我可不想打架

00:02:45.082 --> 00:02:46.083
En garde!
来吧

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.340
-Oh! Sorry.
-Watch it.
-当心点
-对不起

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.343
(clattering)

00:02:57.469 --> 00:02:58.679
Trying to run away?
你还想跑

00:02:58.762 --> 00:03:00.681
We're on a boat, you know.
别忘了这是在船上

00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:02.391
Look, can't we just discuss this?
听着，我们可以谈谈吗？

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.435
That was for stealing,
叫你偷盗

00:03:04.518 --> 00:03:06.061
that was for lying,
叫你撒谎

00:03:06.145 --> 00:03:08.313
and that was for good measure.
叫你长点记性

00:03:09.106 --> 00:03:10.774
(hearty laughter)
叫你长点记性

00:03:10.858 --> 00:03:12.443
That's the spirit!
算你有种，让我们决斗吧

00:03:12.526 --> 00:03:15.404
We have ourselves a duel.
Catch!
算你有种，让我们决斗吧

00:03:15.487 --> 00:03:18.657
Now, come on.
Take your best shot.
好，来吧

00:03:19.408 --> 00:03:21.243
Is that it? Come on, boy.
这算什么，来吧，伙计

00:03:21.326 --> 00:03:24.496
Focus. Focus. Yes!
注意

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.916
Now, stop flapping your wings
like a drunken pelican.
别像喝醉酒的鸭子摆来摆去，站好

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.376
Poise!
别像喝醉酒的鸭子摆来摆去，站好

00:03:30.377 --> 00:03:32.087
Keep your blade up.
Up, up! That's it.
剑拿高点

00:03:32.171 --> 00:03:34.381
-Now...
-(grunting)
来吧

00:03:34.465 --> 00:03:38.844
(Reepicheep grunting and laughing)

00:03:38.927 --> 00:03:41.764
Yoo-hoo! Over here!
在这儿

00:03:41.847 --> 00:03:43.515
Now, lunge with your foot.
注意，我先戳下边

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:45.642
Not your left; your right.
再戳左边，再戳右边

00:03:45.726 --> 00:03:47.019
Got it? Come on.
懂了吗，来吧，麻利点

00:03:47.102 --> 00:03:48.520
Be nimble. Be nimble.
懂了吗，来吧，麻利点

00:03:48.604 --> 00:03:50.564
It's a dance, boy-- a dance.
Come on.
动作要优雅，伙计

00:03:50.647 --> 00:03:52.524
Now, again and again.
优雅，来吧，再来

00:03:52.608 --> 00:03:53.942
That's right. That's right.
再来，很好

00:03:54.026 --> 00:03:55.486
That's... (whimpers)
再来，很好

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:56.945
Oh, no!
不

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.914
And that... is that.
练习…

00:04:06.997 --> 00:04:08.707
-(girl screams)
-(laughter and applause)
到此结束

00:04:12.795 --> 00:04:14.004
Look.
看哪

00:04:16.173 --> 00:04:17.383
Gael?
盖尔

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.510
What are you doing here?
你来这儿干什么？

00:04:26.642 --> 00:04:27.935
Here.
过来

00:04:38.487 --> 00:04:40.697
Looks like we have an extra crew member.
看来我们又多了一位…

00:04:49.206 --> 00:04:51.625
-Welcome aboard.
-Your Majesty.
欢迎上船

00:04:51.709 --> 00:04:54.211
Call me Lucy. Come on.
叫我露西吧

00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:57.715
DRINIAN: Come on, look lively.
Back to work.
好了，别傻站着了

00:04:58.882 --> 00:05:00.175
(men shouting commands)

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:01.677
REEPICHEEP: Good match.
干得不错

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.804
I'll make a swordsman of you yet.
我会把你培养成著名击剑手

00:05:06.014 --> 00:05:09.893
Yes, well, if the playing field
were a little more even,
听着，要是场地能够再平整一些

00:05:09.977 --> 00:05:11.687
would have been
an entirely different result.
最后还不知道谁输谁赢呢

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:14.314
(laughs) Indeed.
是的

00:05:15.816 --> 00:05:18.569
(crewmen shouting commands)

00:05:26.618 --> 00:05:28.162
CASPIAN: It looks uninhabited.
岛上好像无人居住

00:05:28.245 --> 00:05:32.207
But if the lords followed the mist East,
they would have stopped here.
但去海外除妖这是必经之地

00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:34.543
Could be a trap.
也许是陷阱

00:05:35.461 --> 00:05:37.588
EDMUND: Or it could hold some answers.
也许能有些线索

00:05:37.671 --> 00:05:38.881
Caspian?
凯斯宾？

00:05:41.508 --> 00:05:44.553
We'll spend the night on shore,
scour the island in the morning.
我们上岸过夜，明天一早搜索全岛

00:05:44.636 --> 00:05:46.180
Aye, Your Majesty.
遵命，陛下

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.942
(snoring)

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.071
(heavy footsteps thudding)

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:08.243
VOICE (whispering):
Seems they've brought a pig.
好像还有猪的声音

00:06:08.327 --> 00:06:10.370
(snoring)
好像还有猪的声音

00:06:12.456 --> 00:06:15.084
VOICE 2: This one-- it's female.
瞧那个，是女的

00:06:17.002 --> 00:06:18.587
VOICE 3: So's this one.
那个也是

00:06:20.381 --> 00:06:23.550
VOICE 1: This one reads.
这个有文化

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:25.177
VOICE 4: Let's take her.
就是她了

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.179
(gasps)
就是她了

00:06:32.017 --> 00:06:34.269
(muffled shouting)

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.859
(muffled grunting)

